 curvature excludes gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.contact","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.contact_derivatives","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.first_variation"],"evidence_class":"source_argument","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.contact","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives nonnegative tail cost and its vanishing on the support by feasible atom addition and compact fractional mass removal. The first-variation formula and regularity are cited inputs, and the sign conclusion uses minimality.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.contact"},{"claim_id":"support.contact_derivatives","kinds":["derivation"],"rationale":"Derives the value and slope conditions from derivatives of the contact function, with a separate right-hand expansion at zero. The origin argument retains contact at zero when zero belongs to the support and the zero-field identity q(0)=0.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.contact_derivatives"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=contact&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=short&passage=contact"},{"ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/passages/first-variation","stage":"expository","anchor":"first-variation","content_span":{"start_byte":23900,"end_byte":25311,"start_line":557,"end_line":587},"section_ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sections/77","section_title":"Why the SK order parameter has no gaps","claim_refs":["sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.first_variation"],"evidence_class":"source_argument","treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.first_variation","kinds":["statement","explanation"],"rationale":"States the admissible one-sided derivative formula and explains the separate penalty and reoptimised-control contributions. Nonnegativity of the derivative requires a minimiser; the cited formula itself applies to admissible coefficients and feasible directions.","claim_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.first_variation"}],"query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=expository&passage=first-variation&representation=matches","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=expository&passage=first-variation"},{"ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","stage":"expository","anchor":"zero-candidate","content_span":{"start_byte":41626,"end_byte":42764,"start_line":979,"end_line":1015},"section_ref":"sha256:a27286323604d97b33cbece7bb75d3d3291f7d7ec1ed0bfe12af548d92ff72dc/papers/expository.md/sections/41153","section_title":"7. Optional calculations","claim_refs":["sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.diffusion","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.first_variation","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.moment_identity","sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/support.regularity","sha256:c941b